---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { url } from "../lib/paths";
---

<Layout
  title="Where WeCoLab fits"
  description="A plain-language comparison of cooperative app hosting, self-hosting, cloud platforms, private networks and volunteer compute."
>
  <div class="container comparison-page">
    <header class="page-intro comparison-hero">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">A field guide / 01</p>
        <h1>A cloud you build with people you know.</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          What if the spare room for your app belonged to a collaborator, rather than
          a provider you have never met? WeCoLab is being built around that
          question. It makes room for an app at sites people deliberately
          contribute, with the ownership and limits visible to the people
          involved.
        </p>
        <a class="text-link" href={url("docs/architecture/")}>
          See how the fabric works <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
      <aside class="hero-aside" aria-label="The short version">
        <span class="aside-label">The short version</span>
        <p>
          Known people.
          <br />
          Explicit offers.
          <br />
          Persistent apps.
        </p>
        <span class="aside-foot">Not an open auction for compute.</span>
      </aside>
    </header>

    <section class="thesis" aria-labelledby="benchmark-title">
      <div class="section-index">01 / The benchmark</div>
      <div class="section-body">
        <h2 id="benchmark-title">
          The ease is worth borrowing. The business model is different.
        </h2>
        <p>
          <a href="https://www.digitalocean.com/solutions/startups">
            DigitalOcean's pitch to developers
          </a>{" "}
          is a good standard for clarity: spend less time tending
          infrastructure, know roughly what it will cost, and get back to the
          thing you came to build. Its{" "}
          <a href="https://www.digitalocean.com/">current site</a> also puts AI
          infrastructure front and center. The wider platform includes managed
          services, billing, support and provider-operated capacity;{" "}
          <a href="https://www.digitalocean.com/pricing">its pricing page</a>{" "}
          explains the commercial bargain.
        </p>
        <p>
          WeCoLab is after some of that calm, but the hardware comes from a
          small group of people who know one another. The fabric's desired state
          lives in Git at each site. Boxes connect over Nebula; people's devices
          use NetBird. A contributor decides what capacity to offer. That is a
          different operating arrangement, not a promise of DigitalOcean's
          breadth, staffing or service levels.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="landscape" aria-labelledby="landscape-title">
      <div class="section-index">02 / Nearby ideas</div>
      <div class="section-body">
        <h2 id="landscape-title">
          Several good projects solve neighboring problems.
        </h2>
        <p class="section-preface">
          These are differences in emphasis, not a scorecard. You could use more
          than one of these tools together.
        </p>
        <div class="comparison-list">
          <article class="comparison-row">
            <div class="row-category">Run your own services</div>
            <div class="row-content">
              <h3>
                <a href="https://coopcloud.tech/">Co-op Cloud</a> <span>/</span>{" "}
                <a href="https://coolify.io/">Coolify</a> <span>/</span>{" "}
                <a href="https://yunohost.org/">YunoHost</a>
              </h3>
              <p>
                Co-op Cloud brings cooperative operators together around app
                recipes. Coolify makes deploying onto servers you control or
                rent approachable. YunoHost helps people tend services for
                themselves, friends and small groups. WeCoLab starts one step
                earlier: someone in your circle chooses to contribute bounded
                capacity at their site, and your app can be placed across those
                sites. Their deployment and self-hosting work remains valuable.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="comparison-row">
            <div class="row-category">Manage infrastructure</div>
            <div class="row-content">
              <h3>
                <a href="https://linuxcontainers.org/incus/docs/main/">Incus</a>{" "}
                <span>/</span> <a href="https://opennebula.io/">OpenNebula</a>
              </h3>
              <p>
                Incus manages containers and virtual machines, from a host to a
                cluster. OpenNebula addresses private and distributed cloud
                operations, including multi-site infrastructure. Both are
                serious ways to manage compute. WeCoLab is concerned with the
                smaller social and operational unit: which collaborator offered a box,
                which app belongs at which site, and how a group handles a move
                or loss.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="comparison-row">
            <div class="row-category">Connect the people</div>
            <div class="row-content">
              <h3>
                <a href="https://netbird.io/">NetBird</a> <span>/</span>{" "}
                <a href="https://tailscale.com/">Tailscale</a>
              </h3>
              <p>
                These products make private access between devices easier.
                WeCoLab uses NetBird for people's phones and laptops; Nebula
                connects the boxes. A private network is a necessary part of the
                story, but it does not by itself decide who contributes capacity
                or keep an app running at a site.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="comparison-row">
            <div class="row-category">Share distributed capacity</div>
            <div class="row-content">
              <h3>
                <a href="https://akash.network/">Akash</a> <span>/</span>{" "}
                <a href="https://foldingathome.org/">Folding@home</a>{" "}
                <span>/</span> <a href="https://boinc.berkeley.edu/">BOINC</a>
              </h3>
              <p>
                Akash is a public compute marketplace where providers can offer
                capacity to buyers. Folding@home and BOINC recruit volunteer
                machines for scientific work units. WeCoLab is neither a public
                market nor a research-job scheduler. Its proposed exchange is
                reciprocal and deliberately small: persistent apps at sites
                operated by known contributors, within resources they have
                chosen to offer.
              </p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="reality" aria-labelledby="cost-title">
      <div class="section-index">03 / The honest part</div>
      <div class="section-body">
        <h2 id="cost-title">Shared does not mean free, or always on.</h2>
        <div class="reality-columns">
          <p>
            Someone still buys and maintains each machine, pays for power and
            connectivity, looks after updates, and thinks through storage,
            backups and recovery. The design uses a separate object-storage
            vault for database history and backups, so that may carry a bill
            too. A collaborator's outage is a real outage to plan around.
          </p>
          <p>
            There is no managed-cloud SLA hiding inside a collaboration. WeCoLab's
            Git-based fabric, explicit app roles and recovery paths are designed
            to make failures legible and recoverable, not to erase the work of
            operating them. A Mac's idle capacity also has a different
            availability profile from a reserved, persistent app placement.{" "}
            <a href={url("docs/operations/")}>Read the operations guide</a>{" "}
            before trusting it with something important.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="research-note">
          <span>Research note · 30 September 2026</span>
          <p>
            Descriptions of other projects reflect their linked primary websites
            and documentation on this date. This is a comparison of purpose and
            operating model, not a tested feature or performance benchmark.
            WeCoLab's architecture is described in the{" "}
            <a href={url("docs/decisions/")}>design decisions</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <aside class="closing" aria-label="Continue exploring">
      <p>Interested in the work behind the idea?</p>
      <a class="button" href={url("contribute/")}>
        Build with us <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
    </aside>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .comparison-page {
    padding-bottom: 6rem;
  }
  .comparison-hero {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 300px;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 7vw, 7rem);
    align-items: end;
    padding: clamp(4.5rem, 9vw, 9rem) 0 5rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ink);
  }
  .comparison-hero h1 {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 1rem 0 2rem;
    font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 7.7vw, 7.6rem);
    line-height: 0.98;
    letter-spacing: -0.065em;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .lede {
    max-width: 710px;
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 1.8vw, 1.5rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .hero-aside {
    min-height: 270px;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    color: var(--paper);
    background: var(--ink);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: space-between;
  }
  .aside-label,
  .aside-foot,
  .section-index,
  .row-category,
  .research-note span {
    font-family: "IBM Plex Mono", monospace;
    font-size: 0.77rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }
  .aside-label {
    color: #8fc9bb;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .hero-aside p {
    color: var(--paper);
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 2.4vw, 2.1rem);
    line-height: 1.16;
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    margin: 2.5rem 0;
  }
  .aside-foot {
    color: #b8cbc4;
  }
  section.thesis,
  section.landscape,
  section.reality {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(165px, 25%) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 2rem;
    padding: 4.5rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .section-index {
    padding-top: 0.65rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .section-body h2 {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 0 1.6rem;
    font-size: clamp(2.3rem, 4vw, 4.1rem);
    line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.047em;
    font-weight: 500;
    text-wrap: balance;
  }
  .section-body > p {
    max-width: 760px;
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  .section-body a:not(.button),
  .comparison-row a {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
  }
  .section-preface {
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .comparison-list {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--ink);
  }
  .comparison-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(140px, 26%) minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 1.4rem;
    padding: 2.15rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .comparison-row:last-child {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }
  .row-category {
    padding-top: 0.35rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .comparison-row h3 {
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2.3vw, 1.8rem);
    line-height: 1.4;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    margin: 0 0 0.65rem;
  }
  .comparison-row h3 span {
    color: #a2ada4;
    padding: 0 0.15em;
  }
  .comparison-row p {
    max-width: 740px;
    margin: 0;
    line-height: 1.72;
  }
  .reality-columns {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 2rem;
  }
  .reality-columns p {
    margin-top: 0;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
  .research-note {
    max-width: 790px;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    padding: 0.3rem 0 0.3rem 1.4rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .research-note span {
    color: var(--ink);
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .research-note p {
    margin: 0.5rem 0 0;
    line-height: 1.6;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
  .closing {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 2rem;
    padding-top: 4rem;
  }
  .closing p {
    max-width: 670px;
    font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3.5vw, 3.4rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.045em;
    line-height: 1.12;
    margin: 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .comparison-hero {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      padding-top: 4rem;
    }
    .hero-aside {
      min-height: 0;
    }
    .hero-aside p {
      margin: 2rem 0;
    }
    section.thesis,
    section.landscape,
    section.reality {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1rem;
      padding: 3.5rem 0;
    }
    .section-index {
      padding: 0;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    .comparison-hero {
      padding-bottom: 3rem;
    }
    .comparison-hero h1 {
      font-size: clamp(3.2rem, 13vw, 4.8rem);
    }
    .comparison-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0.65rem;
      padding: 1.6rem 0;
    }
    .reality-columns {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 0;
    }
    .closing {
      align-items: start;
      flex-direction: column;
    }
  }
</style>
